  "title": "3-8-08 Sun Cruz 9 rescue",
  "description": "JACKSONVILLE, Fla. - A helicopter crew from Air Station Savannah, Ga., rescue five men from the disabled gambling ship Sun Cruz 9 17-miles off the coast of St. Augustine, Fla., March 8, 2008. The gambling ship left Fort Lauderdale, Fla., for Jacksonville to make repairs when it lost power. The ship then hired another vessel to tow it the rest of the way when the line parted in heavy seas during the night of March 7, 2008. Coast Guard video by Lt. James Willingham, Air Station Savannah.",
